# Code Quality

## Typing
- Strict TypeScript; avoid `any` and untyped escape hatches.
- Prefer explicit return types on exported functions and API handlers.
- Model boundaries with Zod → inferred types.

## Errors
- Fail loudly with typed/domain errors; don’t swallow exceptions.
- Clean `try/catch` with meaningful messages and causes.

```typescript
// ❌ BAD
try { await save(); } catch {}

// ✅ GOOD
try {
  await save();
} catch (e) {
  throw new Error("Failed to save booking", { cause: e });
}
```

## Performance
- Prevent N+1: batch, `include`/`select`, or DataLoader-style fetches.
- Prefer O(1) lookups (`Map`/`Set`) over nested loops when scaling.
- Clean up listeners, intervals, and AbortControllers.
- Lazy-load heavy client components; keep Server Components by default in Next.js.

## Modules
- Small, testable units with clear inputs/outputs.
- Colocate feature code; avoid cross-feature deep imports.
- No dead code or commented-out blocks in commits.
